      "text": "The 61.4 mm reference dimension is treated as the shaft's axial envelope; the extracted 14.25 mm length is treated as an envelope-axis swap with the maximum diameter."
    },
    {
      "assumption_id": "A02",
      "text": "Round bar stock is selected because the part is predominantly rotational and does not require directional grain flow; production quantity 100 alone does not justify forging."
    },
    {
      "assumption_id": "A03",
      "text": "The pre-HT finish_turn_od steps denote controlled soft semi-finishing where hard-turning stock must remain, because the operation vocabulary has no semi-finish OD-turning type."
    },
    {
      "assumption_id": "A04",
      "text": "F01 and F10 are opposed center holes used for workholding, not a functional through-bore; therefore the DIN 8 bore-finishing substitution is not applied as a separate bore cut."
    },
    {
      "assumption_id": "A05",
      "text": "The DIN 8 correction is applied by replacing post-HT face, bore, and OD grinding/honing with one CNC hard-turning setup; gear grinding and teeth honing are omitted entirely."
    },
    {
      "assumption_id": "A06",
      "text": "Case hardening is applied generally without selective masking because the drawing does not identify surfaces that must remain soft."
    },
    {
      "assumption_id": "A07",
      "text": "Post-HT material_hardness_hrc is left null because the drawing specifies 700\u2013800 HV10 and no authoritative HRC value is provided."
    },
    {
      "assumption_id": "A08",
      "text": "The R1 transition F15 is produced incidentally with the adjacent F05 finish-turning profile and does not require a separate form-turning step."
    },
    {
      "assumption_id": "A09",
      "text": "Turning-template rough and finish boring are omitted because no cylindrical functional bore exists; the two center holes are produced by center drilling."
    },
    {
      "assumption_id": "A10",
      "text": "Turning-template threading and part-off steps are omitted because the feature graph contains no thread and individual blanks are saw cut before turning."
    },
    {
      "assumption_id": "A11",
      "text": "Heat-treatment masking and optional post-temper stress relief are omitted because neither selective hardening nor a separate stabilization cycle is specified."
    },
    {
